        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "31cf146f-63c8-4a0e-b08f-8cf2082313c0",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe meet at our designated pick up points and transfer by private coach to our allocated airport for our direct scheduled flight to Nice. On arrival in Nice we are met by our tour manager and travel by private coach to the centrally located 4* Splendid Hotel at Nice for a five night. A welcome dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe visit the Villa and Gardens of Ephrussi de Rothschild for a guided tour this morning. Through the art dealers and experts she befriended, Baroness Ephrussi de Rothschild sought out artworks all over the world, transforming the Villa at Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat into a collector\u2019s paradise. This afternoon we visit Villa E-1027, a modernist villa designed and built between 1926 and 1929, by the Irish architect and furniture designer Eileen Gray.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis morning we visit the Mus\u00E9e Renoir in Cagnes-sur-Mer where Renoir lived for much of the later years of his life and where he took up sculpting for the first time, assisted by Richard Guino and Louis Morel. We then visit Fondation Maeght with its large collection of paintings, sculptures and drawings. Built in 1964 by Paris art dealers Aim\u00E9 and Marguerite Maeght, this is one of Europe\u2019s finest museums of modern art, with paintings by artists such as Bonnard, Braque, Kandinsky and Chagall. The rest of the day is at leisure in Biot, a small fortified medieval hilltop village.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe firstly enjoy a guided tour at the Mus\u00E9e des Beaux Arts. The museum is located in the former home of a Ukrainian princess and displays works sent to Nice by Napoleon after Italy ceded the city to France in 1860. The museum is also home to a fine collection of Impressionist and Post Impressionist paintings by artists such as Renoir, Monet and Dufy. We continue to Mus\u00E9e Marc Chagall, where a guided tour explores its wonderful collection of large paintings, sculptures, stained glass windows, mosaics and tapestries depicting various biblical scenes. Later this afternoon we visit the Franciscan Church and Monastery of Cimiez, where Matisse is buried.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAfter spending some time at leisure in Antibes this morning, we visit the Mus\u00E9e Picasso located in Ch\u00E2teau Grimaldi, a former residence of Monaco\u2019s ruling family. In 1946 the artist used part of the castle as a studio and, in gratitude, donated to the town all 150 works completed during his stay, including \u2018The Goat\u2019. Most works are inspired by the artists\u2019 love of the sea, including \u2018La Joie de Vivre\u2019. A farewell dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 6\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis morning we visit Villa Kerylos. Built between 1902 and 1908 for archaeologist Theodore Reinach in imitation of an ancient Greek residence, it contains lovingly reproduced mosaics, frescoes and furniture. We return to Nice Airport for our direct scheduled flight to the UK, and onwards private coach travel back to our original pick up points.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENB:- Please note we reserve the right to alter the above itinerary if required for operational\nreasons. Given the historic nature of the places visited, a certain degree of walking will be involved, and this holiday may not be suitable for those with mobility problems.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
